  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "Slumdogs of the Caribbean\nThe Caribbean market has been up and down, but more of the latter since the opening of 2009. Though for shipowners near and dear to the West Indies, the simple economics of supply and demand are playing a tougher game these days. Aframaxes and Panamaxes have demonstrated the ability to earn over $60,000 and $50,000 per day; respectively, but have been in the sub-$10,000 per day range recently.",
